{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"category":"Orange Unified Design System","title":"Swift Package integration","role":"project","categoryPathComponent":"Table-Of-Contents-(lime)"},"kind":"project","sections":[{"backgroundImage":"ic_unified_ds.png","image":"ic_unified_ds.png","estimatedTimeInMinutes":10,"kind":"hero","projectFiles":"OUDS-Lime-Tutorial.zip","title":"Swift Package integration","chapter":"Import of the Swift Package and choose its libraries","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 27.1","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDS iOS is exposed through an open source Swift Package hosted on GitHub, and provides several libraries for your needs.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"These libraries help to split products and make users able to select only what they need.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI is the only official supported framework for Apple platforms.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"anchor":"Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries","contentSection":[{"kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS for iOS is an open source Swift Package available on GitHub under MIT license."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The package and the libraries must be added through Xcode."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"title":"Import the Swift Package and the libraries","stepsSection":[{"type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Using Xcode, in your "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"project package dependencies"}]},{"type":"text","text":", add a new "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"dependency"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Search with the GitHub repository URL (https:\/\/github.com\/Orange-OpenSource\/ouds-ios), and select the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ouds-ios"}]},{"type":"text","text":" dependency."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can then choose the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"dependency rule"}]},{"type":"text","text":" you want."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"To know which version you need, you can have a look on the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Orange-OpenSource\/ouds-ios\/wiki\/01-%E2%80%90-Available-API","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and also the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Orange-OpenSource\/ouds-ios\/releases"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Let’s say you will use some release candidate version today, e.g. the version 3.0.0-rc.1"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":"tutorial-lime-1-ouds-swift-package.png","code":null,"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[]},{"type":"step","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you downloaded the package, you will see several libraries are available."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They can be embedded inside your "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"target"}]},{"type":"text","text":" libraries."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Things are separated to let users integrate only what they need and embed the bare minimum of content."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSThemesContract"}]},{"type":"text","text":" library provides the main elements like the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSThemeableView"},{"type":"text","text":". The theme contract is defined inside it."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSThemesOrange"}]},{"type":"text","text":" provides the theme implementation for the Orange products, and contains also assets and all tokens for this theme."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSThemesSosh"}]},{"type":"text","text":" provides the theme implementation for the Sosh products, and contains also assets and all tokens for this theme."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSThemesWireframe"}]},{"type":"text","text":" provides the theme implementation for the Wireframe theme, which is a theme dedicated to mockups and prototypes."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSThemesOrangeCompact"}]},{"type":"text","text":" provides the theme implementation for the Orange products but with constraints of sizes and spaces."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSComponents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" contains the SwiftUI OUDS components defined with the Figma specifications, and also useful view modifers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSTokensRaw"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSTokensSemantic"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSTokensComponents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" are libraries defining and providing the tokens for low level (raw),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"middle level (semantic) or component levels (high level)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSModules"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is for modules or rich components with extra logic."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSFoundations"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is dedicated to some utilities and shared logic."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":"tutorial-lime-1-ouds-libraries.png","code":null,"runtimePreview":null,"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add for example only the umbrella product merging all products mentioned above: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSSwiftUI"}]}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]},{"kind":"assessments","anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding","assessments":[{"type":"multiple-choice","choices":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"I can contribute to OUDS using pull request"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS is open source, under MIT license, and hosted on GitHub. Of course you can contribute!"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS supports officialy all Apple OS like visionOS, tvOS, watchOS, iPadOS, iOS and also CarPlay."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The main supported targets are iOS \/ iPadOS. However we do our best to support macOS, visionOS, tvOS and watchOS."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"CarPlay specific cases are not scoped yet."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS provides UIKit components"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS supports only SwiftUI."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"content":[],"title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Which of these choices is correct?","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"multiple-choice","choices":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some of the available products depending to my needs, or only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSSwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" if I am very lazy and don’t care about my app size."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can import all products provided by the Swift Package, and tailor your choice to keep only the ones needed."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Even if we recommend to choose only the atomic products you need, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSSwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" product wraps all of them."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None, only the Swift package dependency matter."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You need to chose the products the Swift package provides."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"content":[],"title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Which imports of the OUDS Swift Package products can I choose?","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"kind":"callToAction","title":"Introduction","abstract":[{"text":"Welcome to the Lime theme tutorial! In this tutorial, you will learn how to create a custom OUDS theme by overriding tokens from the Orange theme.","type":"text"}],"featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial","action":{"type":"reference","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"Get started","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-2-intro","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"Get started"}}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/tutorials\/oudsthemescontract\/tutorial-lime-1-package-and-libraries"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"modules":[{"projects":[{"sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-1-package-and-libraries#Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-1-package-and-libraries#Check-Your-Understanding"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-1-package-and-libraries"}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(lime)\/Import-of-the-Swift-Package-and-choose-its-libraries"},{"projects":[{"sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc: